virglrenderer: tessellation shader output limits on a GL without atomic counters

What: the caps carry the tessellation control and evaluation shaders' per-vertex output
limits (GL_MAX_TESS_CONTROL_OUTPUT_COMPONENTS and GL_MAX_TESS_EVALUATION_OUTPUT_COMPONENTS,
in vec4s) on every GL with tessellation.
Why: vrend asked for them only on a GL with atomic counters; Apple's GL 4.1 has none, so both
were 0. The guest's Mesa (host_feature_check_version 19 and newer; the host says 23) links
each tessellation shader against them: a whole program whose tessellation shader had any
output failed in the guest ("tessellation control shader uses too many output components
(4 > 0)") and never reached the Mac; only separable tessellation did. The control shader's
limit is the per-vertex one the guest checks (gl_nir_link_varyings.c,
check_against_output_limit); vrend sent the total over all vertices. With this patch whole
tessellation programs reach virgl-shader-clip-distances.patch's last-stage fixes.
Upstream: the same in virglrenderer main (e0a1caf3, checked 2026-10-31: the total, under
atomic counters); not sent.
Test: Tests/virgl/test-whole-program-shapes.c's caps row (both 0 without this patch).

--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -16684,6 +16684,14 @@
    if (has_feature(feat_tessellation)) {
       glGetIntegerv(GL_MAX_TESS_PATCH_COMPONENTS, &max);
       caps->v2.max_shader_patch_varyings = max / 4;
+      /* OmacVM: the per-vertex output limits the guest's Mesa links tessellation shaders
+       * against (host_feature_check_version >= 19); asked under atomic counters before,
+       * which Apple's GL has not: 0, so every whole program with a tessellation shader
+       * that has outputs failed the guest's own link */
+      glGetIntegerv(GL_MAX_TESS_CONTROL_OUTPUT_COMPONENTS, &max);
+      caps->v2.max_tcs_outputs = max / 4;
+      glGetIntegerv(GL_MAX_TESS_EVALUATION_OUTPUT_COMPONENTS, &max);
+      caps->v2.max_tes_outputs = max / 4;
    } else
       caps->v2.max_shader_patch_varyings = 0;
 
@@ -16832,12 +16840,6 @@
                        (GLint*)(caps->v2.max_atomic_counter_buffers + PIPE_SHADER_TESS_CTRL));
          glGetIntegerv(GL_MAX_TESS_EVALUATION_ATOMIC_COUNTER_BUFFERS,
                        (GLint*)(caps->v2.max_atomic_counter_buffers + PIPE_SHADER_TESS_EVAL));
-
-         glGetIntegerv(GL_MAX_TESS_CONTROL_TOTAL_OUTPUT_COMPONENTS, &max);
-         caps->v2.max_tcs_outputs = max / 4;
-
-         glGetIntegerv(GL_MAX_TESS_EVALUATION_OUTPUT_COMPONENTS, &max);
-         caps->v2.max_tes_outputs = max / 4;
       }
 
       if (has_feature(feat_compute_shader)) {
